<title>FRANCE: France seeks approval of sugar sale to Iraq.</title>
<headline>France seeks approval of sugar sale to Iraq.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>France has requested U.N. approval for a recent sale of 50,000 tonnes of French sugar to Iraq under the United Nations oil-for-food deal, a French budget ministry official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The official did not say when the sugar was sold, but U.N. approval is usually sought within several days of a deal being finalised.</p>
<p>Iraq tendered recently for two to four shipments of 12-14,000 tonnes each to arrive in February and March.</p>
</text>
